gpu.c was extracted from the native gputest command encoder. It adapts
VirGL encoding to native Plan 9 C and gpu(3), with a caller-selected device
directory so the same file interface can be bound elsewhere in a namespace.
The Red Hat copyright and MIT permission notice are preserved in LICENSE. No renderer, Mesa, TGSI compiler or Linux
driver is linked into the guest. TGSI text is compiled by host VirGL.
The device tests and generated9 integration use the root LICENSE.

Inline buffer writes reserve payload space without clearing bytes that are
immediately copied over. Headers and final-word padding remain initialized;
gpuemit still returns zeroed parameter words. The cmd path remains synchronous;
gpuflush/gpuwait use the submit/wait files with one kernel-owned request in flight.
